Flushing buffer to disk...
</code></pre> <p>Performance Tip</p> <p>Buffered I/O is especially beneficial for network operations and many small file writes. The default buffer size is 4096 bytes.</p>

The CodeThe ExplanationThe Terminal Output <pre><code>package main

import (
    "bufio"
    "fmt"
    "os"
)

func main() {
    file, err := os.Open("largefile.txt")
    if err != nil {
        fmt.Println("Error:", err)
        return
    }
    defer file.Close()

    // Custom buffer size: 8KB
    scanner := bufio.NewScanner(file)
    scanner.Buffer(make([]byte, 0, 8*1024), 8*1024)

    lineCount := 0
    for scanner.Scan() {
        line := scanner.Text()
        lineCount++

        if lineCount &lt;= 3 {
            fmt.Printf("Line %d: %s\n", lineCount, line[:min(50, len(line))])
        }
    }

    fmt.Printf("\nTotal lines: %d\n", lineCount)
}

func min(a, b int) int {
    if a &lt; b {
        return a
    }
    return b
}
</code></pre> <ul> <li>scanner.Buffer: Sets custom buffer size for scanner</li> <li>Max token size: Second parameter is maximum line length</li> <li>Default: 64KB max token size</li> <li>Large files: Increase buffer for long lines</li> </ul> <pre><code>Line 1: This is the first very long line of the file
